   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "At the restaurant bar, an unfortunate misunderstanding leads Max to accidentally punch his friend Kostya. Full of regret, Max tries to apologize while Kostya nurses a sore nose and asks for fresh juice to clear his head. Meanwhile, the search for Chef Barinov's missing knife is throwing the whole kitchen into turmoil. Listen to their conversation in Russian first, then we will break down each line.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Как-то неловко получилось, Костя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Ты чуть не сломал мне нос!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Старичок, прости меня, пожалуйста!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Зачем мне твоё простое прости?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Теперь за тобой большой долг.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Что я могу сделать для тебя?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Сделай мне свежий апельсиновый сок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "У меня очень кружится голова.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Я сейчас всё быстро сделаю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "На кухне сейчас очень громко.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Шеф опять кричит на поваров?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Он до сих пор ищет нож.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Тогда нам лучше быть тише.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Держи свой сок, друг мой.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let us walk through each line together to understand every expression.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Как-то неловко получилось, Костя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It turned out somewhat awkward, Kostya.' Max acknowledges the uncomfortable situation with an adverbial phrase.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Ты чуть не сломал мне нос!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You almost broke my nose!' An emphatic statement with the adverb meaning nearly or almost.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Старичок, прости меня, пожалуйста!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Old buddy, forgive me, please!' An informal friendly address followed by an apology.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Зачем мне твоё простое прости?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What good is your simple apology to me?' Kostya points out that words alone do not fix a bruised nose.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Теперь за тобой большой долг.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Now you owe me big time.' The noun phrase literally indicates a substantial debt.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Что я могу сделать для тебя?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What can I do for you?' A polite question offering to make amends.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Сделай мне свежий апельсиновый сок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Make me some fresh orange juice.' The imperative specifies what drink will settle his dizziness.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "У меня очень кружится голова.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'My head is spinning very much.' A common Russian physical idiom for feeling dizzy.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Я сейчас всё быстро сделаю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will do everything quickly right now.' Max immediately agrees to prepare the drink.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "На кухне сейчас очень громко.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It is very loud in the kitchen right now.' The neuter short adverb describes the noisy atmosphere.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Шеф опять кричит на поваров?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Is the chef shouting at the cooks again?' The preposition governs the accusative animate plural.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Он до сих пор ищет нож.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'He is still looking for the knife.' The set phrase means up until now or still.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Тогда нам лучше быть тише.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Then it is better for us to be quieter.' Comparative adverbs advise staying under the radar.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Держи свой сок, друг мой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Hold your juice, my friend.' Max hands over the glass with the familiar imperative. Alright, let's hear the whole thing once more.",
